    <Fragment slot="prose">
        <p>
            A 5-stage pipelined MIPS implementation in VHDL. It includes
            hazard detection, forwarding, and custom peripherals, written
            down to the register transfer level.
        </p>
        <p>
            The stages are the classic five: instruction fetch, instruction
            decode, execute, memory, and writeback. That is the pipeline the
            plate draws. This site does not publish the VHDL, a bitstream, or
            a board name.
        </p>
